1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:02,547
India runs on voice notes.

2
00:00:02,897 --> 00:00:06,545
And over a billion Indians have never typed a question to an AI.

3
00:00:06,895 --> 00:00:08,813
For them, voice is the way in.

4
00:00:09,913 --> 00:00:11,235
Listen to a real one.

5
00:00:11,585 --> 00:00:15,686
मेहता जी वाला अपॉइंटमेंट परसों शाम को शिफ्ट करवा दो।
Get the Mehta ji appointment moved to the day after tomorrow, evening.

6
00:00:15,986 --> 00:00:19,991
Six seconds. A doctor, a day, a time, and a job to do.

7
00:00:20,341 --> 00:00:27,063
A speech model hears every word. But who is Mehta ji? When is parso? What does shift karwa do mean?

8
00:00:27,413 --> 00:00:32,848
The base model's answer: a vague suggestion. No doctor, no call, nothing done.

9
00:00:33,948 --> 00:00:36,384
We built Artha for four people.

10
00:00:36,734 --> 00:00:41,511
Aditya, in Hyderabad. Two Rahuls in his phone, and a mother who speaks Telugu.

11
00:00:41,861 --> 00:00:46,819
Sunita, in Pune. To her, tai could mean her house help, or her sister.

12
00:00:47,169 --> 00:00:51,612
Imran, in Lucknow. His customer and his supplier are both called Sharma.

13
00:00:51,962 --> 00:00:56,067
And Meenakshi, in Chennai, who gets a scam call almost every week.

14
00:00:56,417 --> 00:00:59,740
Four languages. One habit. They speak in hints.

15
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:05,534
Equal already answers your calls. Next, it turns voice notes into actions.

16
00:01:05,884 --> 00:01:10,434
That needs a layer that understands what people mean. That's Artha.

17
00:01:10,784 --> 00:01:13,763
Bas ishaara kaafi hai. A hint is enough.

18
00:01:14,863 --> 00:01:16,544
Aditya sends the same note.

19
00:01:16,894 --> 00:01:22,143
Artha knows Mehta ji is his doctor, and parso shaam is Monday at six.

20
00:01:22,493 --> 00:01:26,886
So it offers to call the clinic, with a reminder an hour before. That's his habit.

21
00:01:27,986 --> 00:01:31,478
When a name fits two people, Artha doesn't interrogate you.

22
00:01:31,828 --> 00:01:36,227
Meeting means work, so it picks Rahul Verma, and keeps the cousin one tap away.

23
00:01:37,327 --> 00:01:44,012
He tells his mother he'll come for lunch. Artha writes to her in Telugu, and answers him out loud.

24
00:01:44,362 --> 00:01:47,516
అమ్మ కోసం తెలుగు మెసేజ్ సిద్ధంగా ఉంది.
The message for Amma is ready, in Telugu.

25
00:01:48,316 --> 00:01:55,261
For Imran, dhai hazaar likh do means two thousand five hundred rupees on Sharma ji's account. The customer, not the supplier.

26
00:01:56,361 --> 00:02:02,766
And when a caller asks Meenakshi for her OTP, Artha stops it before any AI sees the digits.

27
00:02:03,866 --> 00:02:07,620
Here's how. Speech recognition, hinted with your contacts' names.

28
00:02:07,970 --> 00:02:12,910
Code that turns parso, dhai sau and repu madhyanam into exact dates and amounts.

29
00:02:13,260 --> 00:02:17,116
A personal knowledge base that pulls up only the people and facts that matter.

30
00:02:17,466 --> 00:02:24,183
One model call that can only pick real contacts. And rules, in code, for money and OTPs.

31
00:02:25,283 --> 00:02:30,456
We tested twenty-nine recordings in seven languages, with every answer written first.

32
00:02:30,806 --> 00:02:36,542
The base model got seventeen percent completely right. With the whole profile pasted in, seventy-nine.

33
00:02:36,892 --> 00:02:38,431
Artha got ninety-seven.

34
00:02:39,931 --> 00:02:46,672
Calls today. Messaging next. Experts after. Artha gives each of them the meaning behind the words.

35
00:02:47,022 --> 00:02:49,280
Artha. Bas ishaara kaafi hai.
